//? Title: Uniform binary search: actual fixed-schedule probes
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Repeated searches in a sorted array can reuse one schedule of descending
strides. The search must still guard each candidate index and distinguish a
missing key from the last key below it.
)

\toc

> The method

Start i=−1. For each descending power-of-two stride s, accept i+s only if it is
in bounds and a[i+s]≤key. The invariant keeps i below or at the rightmost
value≤key, while the remaining strides cover every smaller gap. At termination i
is that rightmost predecessor; equality decides membership. Duplicates therefore
return the rightmost equal index. Actual probes cost O(log n); this checked
convenience API additionally scans ordering and finite values in O(n).

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/uniform_binary_search_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r =
        a::uniform_binary_search_work(std::vector<int>{0, 3, 6, 9, 12}, 9,
                                      a::uniform_search_table(5));
    std::print("| stride | before | probe | accepted | after |\n|---:|---:|---:|---|---:|\n");
    for (auto q : r.probes)
        std::print("|{}|{}|{}|{}|{}|\n", q.step, q.before, q.probe, q.accepted,
                   q.after);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Sorted keys0,3,6,9,12; target9");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual scheduled probes",
                                     r.probes.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual match index {}", r.index));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/uniform_binary_search_tiny.svg");
}
```
